{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-22567","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23013","text":"Dual- and Triple-Loop Machine Architecture"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22569","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23014","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE update (OS-010, 2026-04):"},{"id":"spn-23015","text":" With the introduction of OS-010 PULSE, the loop-interlock pattern documented here is now formalized as a manifest standard. Graphonomous, PRISM, AgenTroMatic, and every other portfolio loop declare their phases in "},{"id":"spn-23016","marks":["code"],"text":"<loop>.pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-23017","text":" files (see "},{"id":"spn-23018","marks":["code"],"text":"/PULSE/manifests/"},{"id":"spn-23019","text":"), validated against "},{"id":"spn-23020","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-23021","text":". The \"dual loop\" is a special case of arbitrarily nestable PULSE loops — the same machine grouping works at any depth, and PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-23022","marks":["code"],"text":"interact"},{"id":"spn-23023","text":" phase reads the inner system's PULSE manifest to discover the "},{"id":"spn-23024","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-23025","text":" boundary at runtime rather than hard-coding the integration. See \"Triple loop and beyond\" below."}]}],"id":"blk-22568","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-22570","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23026","text":"Overview"}]},{"id":"blk-22571","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23027","text":"PRISM and Graphonomous are both closed-loop systems. When PRISM evaluates Graphonomous, their loops interlock — the outer loop (PRISM) improves the benchmark while the inner loop (Graphonomous) improves the memory. Each makes the other sharper."}]},{"id":"blk-22572","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23028","text":"The machine architecture solves the tool explosion problem: 47 PRISM tools + 29 Graphonomous tools = 76 tools in a shared session. Research shows tool selection accuracy degrades to ~49% at that scale, and schema overhead burns 40-80K tokens."}]},{"id":"blk-22573","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23029","marks":["bold"],"text":"Solution:"},{"id":"spn-23030","text":" Group tools by loop phase, not category. 6 PRISM machines + 5 Graphonomous machines = 11 tools. Selection accuracy jumps to ~95%."}]},{"id":"blk-22574","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23031","text":"The Interlocking Loops"}]},{"id":"blk-22575","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Graphonomous (memory loop)          PRISM (evaluation loop)\n──────────────────────────          ───────────────────────\nretrieve  \"What do I know?\"         compose    \"What should I test?\"\nroute     \"What should I do?\"       interact   \"Run the test\"\nact       \"Do it\"                   observe    \"Judge the result\"\nlearn     \"Did it work?\"            reflect    \"What should change?\"\nconsolidate \"Clean up\"              diagnose   \"What's actionable?\""},{"id":"blk-22576","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23032","text":"When PRISM benchmarks Graphonomous:"}]},{"id":"blk-22577","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"PRISM compose ──→ PRISM interact ──→ PRISM observe ──→ PRISM reflect ──→ PRISM diagnose\n                       │\n                       ▼\n              ┌─── Graphonomous ───┐\n              │  retrieve → route  │\n              │  → act → learn     │\n              │  → consolidate     │\n              └────────────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-22578","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23033","text":"PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-23034","marks":["code"],"text":"interact"},{"id":"spn-23035","text":" phase drives the system-under-test through its own closed loop. PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-23036","marks":["code"],"text":"observe"},{"id":"spn-23037","text":" phase judges how well that inner loop performed. PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-23038","marks":["code"],"text":"reflect"},{"id":"spn-23039","text":" phase evolves scenarios based on where the inner loop failed."}]},{"id":"blk-22579","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23040","text":"PRISM: 47 tools → 6 machines"}]},{"id":"blk-22580","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23041","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-23042","text":" — \"What should I test?\" (9 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22581","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23043","marks":["code"],"text":"scenarios"},{"id":"spn-23044","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23045","marks":["code"],"text":"validate"},{"id":"spn-23046","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23047","marks":["code"],"text":"list"},{"id":"spn-23048","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23049","marks":["code"],"text":"get"},{"id":"spn-23050","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23051","marks":["code"],"text":"retire"},{"id":"spn-23052","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23053","marks":["code"],"text":"import"},{"id":"spn-23054","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23055","marks":["code"],"text":"byor_register"},{"id":"spn-23056","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23057","marks":["code"],"text":"byor_discover"},{"id":"spn-23058","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23059","marks":["code"],"text":"byor_generate"}]},{"id":"blk-22582","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23060","marks":["code"],"text":"interact"},{"id":"spn-23061","text":" — \"Run the test\" (8 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22583","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23062","marks":["code"],"text":"run"},{"id":"spn-23063","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23064","marks":["code"],"text":"run_sequence"},{"id":"spn-23065","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23066","marks":["code"],"text":"run_matrix"},{"id":"spn-23067","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23068","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-23069","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23070","marks":["code"],"text":"transcript"},{"id":"spn-23071","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23072","marks":["code"],"text":"cancel"},{"id":"spn-23073","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23074","marks":["code"],"text":"byor_evaluate"},{"id":"spn-23075","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23076","marks":["code"],"text":"byor_compare"}]},{"id":"blk-22584","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23077","marks":["code"],"text":"observe"},{"id":"spn-23078","text":" — \"Judge the result\" (5 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22585","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23079","marks":["code"],"text":"judge_transcript"},{"id":"spn-23080","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23081","marks":["code"],"text":"judge_dimension"},{"id":"spn-23082","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23083","marks":["code"],"text":"meta_judge"},{"id":"spn-23084","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23085","marks":["code"],"text":"meta_judge_batch"},{"id":"spn-23086","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23087","marks":["code"],"text":"override"}]},{"id":"blk-22586","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23088","marks":["code"],"text":"reflect"},{"id":"spn-23089","text":" — \"What should change?\" (7 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22587","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23090","marks":["code"],"text":"analyze_gaps"},{"id":"spn-23091","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23092","marks":["code"],"text":"evolve"},{"id":"spn-23093","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23094","marks":["code"],"text":"advance_cycle"},{"id":"spn-23095","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23096","marks":["code"],"text":"calibrate_irt"},{"id":"spn-23097","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23098","marks":["code"],"text":"cycle_history"},{"id":"spn-23099","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23100","marks":["code"],"text":"byor_recommend"},{"id":"spn-23101","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23102","marks":["code"],"text":"byor_infer_profile"}]},{"id":"blk-22588","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23103","marks":["code"],"text":"diagnose"},{"id":"spn-23104","text":" — \"What's actionable?\" (13 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22589","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23105","marks":["code"],"text":"report"},{"id":"spn-23106","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23107","marks":["code"],"text":"failure_patterns"},{"id":"spn-23108","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23109","marks":["code"],"text":"retest"},{"id":"spn-23110","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23111","marks":["code"],"text":"verify"},{"id":"spn-23112","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23113","marks":["code"],"text":"regressions"},{"id":"spn-23114","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23115","marks":["code"],"text":"suggest_fixes"},{"id":"spn-23116","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23117","marks":["code"],"text":"leaderboard"},{"id":"spn-23118","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23119","marks":["code"],"text":"leaderboard_history"},{"id":"spn-23120","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23121","marks":["code"],"text":"compare_systems"},{"id":"spn-23122","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23123","marks":["code"],"text":"dimension_leaders"},{"id":"spn-23124","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23125","marks":["code"],"text":"fit_recommendation"},{"id":"spn-23126","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23127","marks":["code"],"text":"compare_fit"},{"id":"spn-23128","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23129","marks":["code"],"text":"task_profiles"}]},{"id":"blk-22590","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23130","marks":["code"],"text":"config"},{"id":"spn-23131","text":" — Admin/setup (5 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22591","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23132","marks":["code"],"text":"set_weights"},{"id":"spn-23133","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23134","marks":["code"],"text":"register_system"},{"id":"spn-23135","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23136","marks":["code"],"text":"list_systems"},{"id":"spn-23137","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23138","marks":["code"],"text":"get_config"},{"id":"spn-23139","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23140","marks":["code"],"text":"create_profile"}]},{"id":"blk-22592","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23141","text":"Graphonomous: 29 tools → 5 machines"}]},{"id":"blk-22593","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23142","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-23143","text":" — \"What do I know?\" (6 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22594","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23144","marks":["code"],"text":"context"},{"id":"spn-23145","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23146","marks":["code"],"text":"episodic"},{"id":"spn-23147","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23148","marks":["code"],"text":"procedural"},{"id":"spn-23149","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23150","marks":["code"],"text":"coverage"},{"id":"spn-23151","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23152","marks":["code"],"text":"trace_evidence"},{"id":"spn-23153","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23154","marks":["code"],"text":"frontier"}]},{"id":"blk-22595","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23155","marks":["code"],"text":"route"},{"id":"spn-23156","text":" — \"What should I do?\" (5 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22596","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23157","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"},{"id":"spn-23158","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23159","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberate"},{"id":"spn-23160","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23161","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_survey"},{"id":"spn-23162","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23163","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_cycle"},{"id":"spn-23164","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23165","marks":["code"],"text":"review_goal"}]},{"id":"blk-22597","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23166","marks":["code"],"text":"act"},{"id":"spn-23167","text":" — \"Do it\" (9 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22598","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23168","marks":["code"],"text":"store_node"},{"id":"spn-23169","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23170","marks":["code"],"text":"store_edge"},{"id":"spn-23171","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23172","marks":["code"],"text":"delete_node"},{"id":"spn-23173","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23174","marks":["code"],"text":"manage_edge"},{"id":"spn-23175","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23176","marks":["code"],"text":"manage_goal"},{"id":"spn-23177","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23178","marks":["code"],"text":"belief_revise"},{"id":"spn-23179","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23180","marks":["code"],"text":"forget_node"},{"id":"spn-23181","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23182","marks":["code"],"text":"forget_policy"},{"id":"spn-23183","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23184","marks":["code"],"text":"gdpr_erase"}]},{"id":"blk-22599","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23185","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-23186","text":" — \"Did it work?\" (5 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22600","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23187","marks":["code"],"text":"from_outcome"},{"id":"spn-23188","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23189","marks":["code"],"text":"from_feedback"},{"id":"spn-23190","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23191","marks":["code"],"text":"detect_novelty"},{"id":"spn-23192","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23193","marks":["code"],"text":"from_interaction"},{"id":"spn-23194","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23195","marks":["code"],"text":"contradictions"}]},{"id":"blk-22601","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23196","marks":["code"],"text":"consolidate"},{"id":"spn-23197","text":" — \"Clean up\" (4 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22602","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23198","marks":["code"],"text":"run"},{"id":"spn-23199","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23200","marks":["code"],"text":"stats"},{"id":"spn-23201","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23202","marks":["code"],"text":"query"},{"id":"spn-23203","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23204","marks":["code"],"text":"traverse"}]},{"id":"blk-22603","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23205","text":"Combined Impact"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-22605","spans":[{"id":"spn-23206","text":"Scenario"}]},{"id":"blk-22606","spans":[{"id":"spn-23207","text":"Before"}]},{"id":"blk-22607","spans":[{"id":"spn-23208","text":"After"}]}],"id":"blk-22604","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-22608","spans":[{"id":"spn-23209","text":"Graphonomous alone"}]},{"id":"blk-22609","spans":[{"id":"spn-23210","text":"29 tools"}]},{"id":"blk-22610","spans":[{"id":"spn-23211","text":"5 tools"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22611","spans":[{"id":"spn-23212","text":"PRISM alone"}]},{"id":"blk-22612","spans":[{"id":"spn-23213","text":"47 tools"}]},{"id":"blk-22613","spans":[{"id":"spn-23214","text":"6 tools"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22614","spans":[{"id":"spn-23215","text":"Both in same session"}]},{"id":"blk-22615","spans":[{"id":"spn-23216","text":"76 tools"}]},{"id":"blk-22616","spans":[{"id":"spn-23217","text":"11 tools"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-22617","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23218","text":"Context savings: ~85% reduction in tool schema tokens. Selection accuracy: from ~49% (76 tools) to ~95% (11 tools)."}]},{"id":"blk-22618","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23219","text":"Implementation"}]},{"id":"blk-22619","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23220","text":"Both systems use the same Elixir pattern: a single Anubis.Server.Component module per machine with an "},{"id":"spn-23221","marks":["code"],"text":"action"},{"id":"spn-23222","text":" field that dispatches internally to the existing tool implementations. The v1 tool modules are preserved as the implementation layer."}]},{"id":"blk-22620","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23223","text":"See:"}]},{"id":"blk-22621","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22623","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23224","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous/lib/graphonomous/mcp/machines/"},{"id":"spn-23225","text":" — Graphonomous machine modules"}]}],"id":"blk-22622","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22625","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23226","marks":["code"],"text":"PRISM/lib/prism/mcp/machines/"},{"id":"spn-23227","text":" — PRISM machine modules"}]}],"id":"blk-22624","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22627","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23228","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/prompts/DUAL_LOOP_MACHINES.md"},{"id":"spn-23229","text":" — canonical architecture design"}]}],"id":"blk-22626","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-22628","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23230","text":"Triple loop and beyond — PULSE generalization"}]},{"id":"blk-22629","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23231","text":"The Graphonomous ↔ PRISM dual loop is the canonical example, but the [&] ecosystem actually runs "},{"id":"spn-23232","marks":["bold"],"text":"at least three"},{"id":"spn-23233","text":" nested loops today:"}]},{"id":"blk-22630","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"PRISM (outer)        compose → interact → observe → reflect → diagnose\n  │\n  └─ Graphonomous    retrieve → route → act → learn → consolidate\n       │\n       └─ Deliberation    survey → triage → dispatch → act → learn"},{"id":"blk-22631","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23234","text":"OS-010 PULSE encodes this nesting in each manifest's "},{"id":"spn-23235","marks":["code"],"text":"nesting"},{"id":"spn-23236","text":" block:"}]},{"id":"blk-22632","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22634","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23237","marks":["code"],"text":"prism.benchmark"},{"id":"spn-23238","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-23239","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [graphonomous.continual_learning]"}]}],"id":"blk-22633","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22636","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23240","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.continual_learning"},{"id":"spn-23241","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-23242","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [graphonomous.deliberate]"},{"id":"spn-23243","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-23244","marks":["code"],"text":"parent_loop: prism.benchmark"}]}],"id":"blk-22635","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22638","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23245","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.deliberate"},{"id":"spn-23246","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-23247","marks":["code"],"text":"parent_loop: graphonomous.continual_learning"}]}],"id":"blk-22637","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-22639","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23248","text":"PULSE supports unbounded nesting depth. OS-008 (Agent Harness, draft) is expected to add a fourth outer layer that wraps PRISM itself — when it ships, the only change required is a new manifest with "},{"id":"spn-23249","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [prism.benchmark]"},{"id":"spn-23250","text":". No code changes to existing machines."}]},{"id":"blk-22640","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23251","text":"Why this matters for the machine architecture"}]},{"id":"blk-22641","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23252","text":"The 5/6/11-tool count documented above is a "},{"id":"spn-23253","marks":["bold"],"text":"floor"},{"id":"spn-23254","text":", not a ceiling. Adding a third loop adds at most 5 more machines (one per phase kind), and because PULSE manifests declare the inner-loop boundary explicitly, the outer machines do not need to learn about inner machines individually. PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-23255","marks":["code"],"text":"interact"},{"id":"spn-23256","text":" machine, for example, drives any PULSE-conforming inner loop through its declared "},{"id":"spn-23257","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-23258","text":" phase — it does not need a Graphonomous-specific code path."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-22643","spans":[{"id":"spn-23259","text":"Layers in session"}]},{"id":"blk-22644","spans":[{"id":"spn-23260","text":"Tool count (machines)"}]},{"id":"blk-22645","spans":[{"id":"spn-23261","text":"Tool count (legacy v1)"}]}],"id":"blk-22642","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-22646","spans":[{"id":"spn-23262","text":"Graphonomous alone"}]},{"id":"blk-22647","spans":[{"id":"spn-23263","text":"5"}]},{"id":"blk-22648","spans":[{"id":"spn-23264","text":"29"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22649","spans":[{"id":"spn-23265","text":"Graphonomous + PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-22650","spans":[{"id":"spn-23266","text":"11"}]},{"id":"blk-22651","spans":[{"id":"spn-23267","text":"76"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22652","spans":[{"id":"spn-23268","text":"Graphonomous + PRISM + OS-008 Harness"}]},{"id":"blk-22653","spans":[{"id":"spn-23269","text":"~16"}]},{"id":"blk-22654","spans":[{"id":"spn-23270","text":"~100+"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22655","spans":[{"id":"spn-23271","text":"Graphonomous + PRISM + OS-008 + AgenTroMatic deliberation"}]},{"id":"blk-22656","spans":[{"id":"spn-23272","text":"~21"}]},{"id":"blk-22657","spans":[{"id":"spn-23273","text":"~130+"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-22658","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23274","text":"The savings compound with depth, and PULSE's manifest standard is what makes the composition algebraic instead of ad-hoc."}]},{"id":"blk-22659","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23275","text":"Three-protocol stack at runtime"}]},{"id":"blk-22660","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  PRISM    — measures loops over time      (diagnostic)   │ OS-009\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  PULSE    — declares loops + circulation   (temporal)    │ OS-010\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [&]      — composes capabilities          (structural)  │ AmpersandBoxDesign\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-22661","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23276","text":"A loop is "},{"id":"spn-23277","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE-conforming"},{"id":"spn-23278","text":" if its manifest validates against "},{"id":"spn-23279","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-23280","text":" and its runtime passes all 12 conformance tests. A system is "},{"id":"spn-23281","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM-evaluable"},{"id":"spn-23282","text":" automatically once it is PULSE-conforming — PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-23283","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-23284","text":" phase reads the manifest, injects scenarios at the declared "},{"id":"spn-23285","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-23286","text":" boundary, and observes outcomes via the declared "},{"id":"spn-23287","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-23288","text":" phase. No bespoke per-system integration required."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierasp2rzpe2givscufqwq4ts2mguoroj3q3w5bg6z4fdcbgmcyfttha","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}